a. prevent all forms of violence against women and children;
b. provide protection and services to women and children victims of gender-based violence;
c. provide a sense of security to women and children victims of violence;
d. restore the physical, psychological and economic condition of women and children victims of violence; and
e. take action against perpetrators of violence against women and children.

Article 27
(1) Efforts to prevent violence against Women and Children shall be carried out in an integrated manner by Regional Apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. PPPA;
b. social affairs;
c. health;
d. education;
e. manpower;
f. population and civil registration;
g. law;
h. cooperatives and micro enterprises;
i. mental and spiritual; and
j. peace and order.
(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by means of:
a. building cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, as well as Educational Institutions, Health institutions, hospitals, various NGOs that care about women and children;
b. building participation and awareness of the community, family, towards the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
c. establishing a violence prevention system that provides a complete and easily accessible information system;
d. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence;
e. providing critical education about the rights of women and children as victims of violence to the community; and
f. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(3) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the RPJPD and RPJMD.

Article 55
In order to achieve the objective of protection of women (1) and child victims of acts of violence, the Regional Government may conduct cooperation with:
a. central government;
b. provincial government;
c. other regency/city government;
d. law enforcement institutions/ and/or law enforcement officers;
e. non-governmental organizations;
f. community;
g. universities/ academics; and
h. mass media.
The cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: (2)
a. exchange of data and information;
b. recovery of victims of acts of violence;
c. repatriation and social reintegration;
d. provision of evidence and witnesses; and
e. followed up in accordance with applicable law.
The cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (3) (2) shall be set forth in the form of a cooperation agreement in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 9
Neglect within the household as referred to in Article 5 letter d, includes:
a. acts of deliberately neglecting a woman within the scope of the household, whereas according to the law applicable to him or due to agreement or contract he is obligated to provide livelihood and care to the said woman;
b. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of a child properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or other parties responsible for their care;
c. acts of deliberately neglecting to care for or look after a child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care; and
d. deliberate neglect of a child who still requires care by their biological mother in order to become an Indonesian Migrant Worker abroad.

